From: thelamer <ryankuba@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:48:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Code a picture whose forced quantizer is 0 at the
 sequence's

use_qp_file forces the quantizer of every picture, so a caller that names one for some pictures
names one for all, and a forced quantizer codes the picture at it whatever its temporal layer,
where the sequence's quantizer codes each layer at its own offset. A picture whose qp is 0, which
the forced path took as 1 since the real-time mode codes nothing lossless, now takes the
sequence's path as without use_qp_file, so a caller forces only the pictures it means to:
SVT_AV1_QP_FILE_KEEPS_SEQUENCE says the library does.

A session that names qp 0 for every picture comes out bit for bit as without use_qp_file, at
1280x720 in the real-time low-delay mode, layered and flat, with a constant-block map and
without.
---
 Source/API/EbSvtAv1Enc.h                         | 4 +++-
 Source/Lib/Codec/resource_coordination_process.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/API/EbSvtAv1Enc.h b/Source/API/EbSvtAv1Enc.h
index 2cde987..66aa2db 100644
--- a/Source/API/EbSvtAv1Enc.h
+++ b/Source/API/EbSvtAv1Enc.h
@@ -409,7 +409,9 @@ typedef struct EbSvtAv1EncConfiguration {
      * Default is 50. */
     uint32_t qp;
 
-    /* force qp values for every picture that are passed in the header pointer
+#define SVT_AV1_QP_FILE_KEEPS_SEQUENCE 1
+    /* force qp values for every picture that are passed in the header pointer;
+    * a picture whose qp is 0 is coded as it would be without this
     *
     * Default is 0.*/
     bool use_qp_file;
diff --git a/Source/Lib/Codec/resource_coordination_process.c b/Source/Lib/Codec/resource_coordination_process.c
index ffc8f12..e16cb06 100644
--- a/Source/Lib/Codec/resource_coordination_process.c
+++ b/Source/Lib/Codec/resource_coordination_process.c
@@ -1357,7 +1357,7 @@ EbErrorType svt_aom_resource_coordination_kernel_iter(void* context) {
                 SVT_LOG("Error reading data in multi pass encoding\n");
             }
         }
-        if (scs->static_config.use_qp_file) {
+        if (scs->static_config.use_qp_file && pcs->input_ptr->qp != 0) {
             pcs->qp_on_the_fly = true;
             if (pcs->input_ptr->qp > MAX_QP_VALUE) {
                 SVT_WARN("INPUT QP/CRF OUTSIDE OF RANGE\n");
